# Panel Shell UX (Permanent)

## Law

Authenticated product chrome is a **sidebar + header panel**, not a top link farm.

| Surface | Layout |
| --- | --- |
| Public / marketing / login / share / web profile | Lightweight chrome (no full nav) |
| Authenticated `/app/*` | **Sidebar** (primary nav) + **compact header** + page stage |

## Auth chrome

- Unauthenticated visit to `/app/**` → redirect **login** (existing `RequireAuth`).
- Successful login → **`/app`** (panel home).
- **Logout** always visible in panel (sidebar footer or header); clears session + active business → `/login`.
- Authenticated user on `/login` → redirect to `/app`.

## Sidebar

- **Minimal:** grouped links, quiet labels, one active indicator — no dense icon rainbow.
- **Business switcher** lives at the **top of the sidebar** (not in the header link row). Custom popover/list — not a bare native `<select>` as the only UX.
- Collapse on small viewports (drawer / overlay); header hamburger.
- Theme + locale remain reachable (header or sidebar footer).

## Header

- Four icon actions only: **personal profile**, **business profile** (branding), **theme**, **locale**.
- No duplicate full nav in the header; optional collapse control for the sidebar.

## Page transitions

- Route changes inside `/app` animate the main stage (opacity + short translate, ~320–420ms, shared easing with auth wizard).
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
- Do not remount the whole shell on every navigation (sidebar stays put).

## Theme / i18n

- Tokens only (`10-theme-and-i18n.mdc`); fa + en keys for all new chrome strings; RTL-aware sidebar placement (`inline-start`).

## Forbidden

- Returning to a wrap-heavy top navbar of every feature link.
- Putting business switcher only in an unreachable overflow header.
- Hard-coded marketing purple/glow chrome that ignores tokens.
